  "construction_notes": [
    {
      "text": "Parcel match: sources give 249-66-009 and -010, merged under T22-033 and no longer in county data. 249-66-054 (county situs 1281 E Julian St) is 0.97 acre, the stated site size, between 1251 and 1299 E Julian. Matched by location and area, not the source's own APN.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001878",
        "SRC-001875"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Split out of SCC-000027, where state report rows combined it with 2388 S Bascom.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001635"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "YIMBY reports the two parcels bought for $8.15 million in Aug. 2025.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001877"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "City of San Jose permit H22-034 (Site Development Permit/Amendment, folder year 2022), status Approved, issue date 2024-01-10: \"Site Development Permit to demolish two single-family houses and remove 50 trees, including 18 ordinance-size trees, for the construction of a seven-story residential building with podium parking and 140 units, including 14 units restricted to very-low-in\" (city text cut off at 255 characters)",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001956"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "City of San Jose permit T22-033 (Tentative Map, folder year 2022), status Approved: \"Vesting Tentative Map to reconfigure two parcels into one parcel and allow up to 140 residential condominiums on an approximately 0.98-gross acre site.\"",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001956"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "CTCAC staff report (Aug. 2024) showed construction financing from U.S. Bank ($65.4M tax-exempt, $11.25M recycled tax-exempt, $13M taxable) and a $38.36M CalHFA tax-exempt permanent loan. CalHFA's final commitment report (May 2025) shows Banc of California as construction lender and Palm Drive Associates, LLC as tax credit investor, replacing U.S. Bank and Walker & Dunlop.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001635",
        "SRC-001875"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "CTCAC recommended $6,379,444 in annual federal credits, $36,054,485 in total state credits and $65,400,000 in tax-exempt bond cap.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001635"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Site held one single-family home and one duplex; the seller was to relocate residents before transfer.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001875"
      ]
    }
  ],
